-different ID and must be reviewed and repinned; the runner refuses it by
-default and launches by that ID, not the mutable tag. The run workspace's
-`.git` is writable agent output: file snapshots and resume checks exclude it.
-No host Git command may trust its configuration, hooks, refs, or object store
-without separate verification in an isolated host-owned repository. The run
-workspace also has no disk quota; the 64 MiB snapshot limit does not bound
-`.git` growth. A network-disabled, read-only inspection showed Git 2.39.5 and
-Codex CLI 0.159.2 in this image. No model turn was run.
